 "notes": "The shared WebSearch budget ran out early, so almost all work was WebFetch of known pages (Wikipedia incl. its reference lists, Kirkus, Time archive, UPI, THES, Sunday Times of Sri Lanka, lakdiva.org.lk, IEEE Spectrum, the Clarke Foundation, sfadb). ISFDB, the Locus index, SF Encyclopedia, Fancyclopedia, NYT, BBC, Guardian, New Yorker, Wired and web.archive.org could not be fetched. Months for most books after 1973 could not be verified because Wikipedia gives only the year. BOOK MONTHS: Kirkus entries with an explicit day (not the 1st or 15th) are used as publication dates for 1957-1973 and 1977 (confirmed); entries on the 1st/15th are only review-issue dates and are marked to confirm. Kirkus dates for later books are visibly unreliable (Imperial Earth Jan 1975, Fountains Jan 1978, Songs of Distant Earth Apr 1987), so they were not used as proof. NEWS/CITATION CELLS: for the NYT (1973-08, 1986-05), New Yorker (1969-08), BBC (1998-01, 1998-04, 2000-05), Guardian (1999-09, 2000-09), The Island (2000-12), A.V. Club (2004-02), Popular Science (2004-08), Playboy (1972-01, 1986-07) and Ukrainian Weekly (1984-04, issue dated 8 Apr 1984 per Scribd) items, the date comes from the citation in a Wikipedia reference list I opened; I could not open the article itself, so treat the headline wording as drawn from the citation title. AWARDS: Hugo and Nebula months are marked to confirm. Worldcon dates straddle Aug/Sep (1956 31 Aug-3 Sep; 1974 29 Aug-2 Sep; 1980 29 Aug-1 Sep; 1969 28 Aug-1 Sep) and no ceremony date was found; Nebula ceremony dates were not found (April used as placeholder). The 1969 Hugo for 2001 (Dramatic Presentation) is omitted because August 1969 holds the dated New Yorker profile. SFWA Grand Master is 1986 per SFWA, month unknown (August is the old placeholder). Kalinga Prize: lists give 1961, UNESCO Courier says 1962 award; month unknown. Stuart Ballantine Medal 1963, month unknown. Marconi 1982, month unknown. CONFLICTS RESOLVED: Ceylon arrival is January 1956 per the Sunday Times of Sri Lanka (16 Dec 2007), other sources say Dec 1955. 2010: Odyssey Two is Dec 1982 per Wikipedia infobox (Kirkus issue Nov 1982). The Light of Other Days is Apr 2000 per Wikipedia (Kirkus 24 Feb 2000). Rama Revealed is Oct 1993 (UK) vs Kirkus Feb 1994. The Garden of Rama is Sept 1991. 2001 novel is June 1968. Knighthood was gazetted 30 Dec 1997 but BBC reported it 1 Jan 1998, so the cell sits in 1998-01 and the 80th birthday is in 1997-12. 2061 is Dec 1987 per Wikipedia (UK). SINGLE-SOURCE: the Great Basses wreck date (22 Mar 1961) and the Ceylon Astronomical Society (June 1959 on one lakdiva page, 1960 on another, so omitted) come from Kavan Ratnatunga's lakdiva.org.lk pages; Wikipedia gives only the year 1961. The Nehru Memorial Address (Nov 1986) comes from a photo caption on the Clarke Foundation page. Heinlein Award 2004-05 is the 22 May 2004 press-release date cited on Wikipedia. THIN AREAS: 1975-1976, 1978, 1981, 1983, 1987-1988, 1995, 2001-2002, 2006 have little or nothing verifiable; the SDI testimony (1984), polio (1962), post-polio diagnosis (1988), Marilyn Mayfield's death (1991), McAleer biography (1992), resident guest status (1975) are year-only facts kept at their old placeholder months. Nothing from memory was marked confirmed. percent_confirmed is confirmed cells divided by 627 months."
